==Battleground==
*1 [[Relic Bun-Bun]] spawns as the boss after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[M. Ost]] spawns as the boss after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Othom]] spawns as the boss after 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The enemy limit is one, so the other threats can't spawn unless the previous enemy has been defeated.

It's possible to [[cheese]] this stage by meatshielding against Othom while units with [[Long Distance]] slowly destroy it. One strategy involves using any fast meatshield, such as [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] or [[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Riceball Cat]], to stall it while [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cats]] snipe the enemy base.

To fight this stage traditionally, you'll need to bring counters to each of the triple threat. Dealing with Othom is simple enough, as it's easily stalled. [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Schoolbus Nyandam]] can outrange it, but timing fast and hard-hitting units like [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] work as well. M. Ost and Relic Bun-Bun have significantly more pushing power. However, [[Talents|Talented]] [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Rodeo Cat]] combined with Future Cat ensure both M. Ost and Relic Bun-Bun are unable to push meaningfully. Cleaning up these enemies can be done in the same way as for Othom.

=== Recommended Ubers ===

* [[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]]: Just as she shreds the rest of [[Uncanny Legends]], she easily outranges every threat in the stage while providing incredibly powerful [[Freeze]] and [[Explosion|Explosions]]. Since she's also [[Strong]] against [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic enemies]], she'll be able to take a beating if your frontline gives out for a moment.
* [[Trixi the Merc (Uber Rare Cat)|Trixi the Revenant]]: While not being able to outrange M. Ost or Othom, her Strong against Relics and incredible Freeze ability allows her to be a more high-risk high-reward version of Lunacia.

